# ${title}

${description}

This folder is a standalone LangChain and LangGraph project, exported from the awa blueprint
`${blueprint}`. It runs without awa installed. The export is one-way: nothing syncs back, so
from here on you change the code in this folder, with LangChain and LangGraph only. If you want
to keep the awa project as the source of truth, keep working in the blueprint and export again
into a new folder.

## Run

```console
$$ python -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -e ".[dev]"      # Windows: .venv\Scripts\pip
$$ cp .env.example .env                                           # then add the model's key
$$ python run.py "your task"
```

`run.py` runs the agent once with an in-memory checkpointer and asks on the terminal when a tool
call needs approval. `langgraph dev` serves the graph in LangGraph Studio (`langgraph.json`).

## Test

```console
$$ pytest
```

The tests are offline: a scripted chat model (`tests/fakes.py`) stands in for the real one.

## Where things are

| File | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `src/${package}/graph.py` | the agent, built with `create_agent`; `build_graph(model, checkpointer)` and `graph` |
| `src/${package}/settings.py` | the model id (override with the variable `MODEL`), its settings and the run limits |
| `src/${package}/prompts/${agent}.md` | the system prompt, frozen as awa rendered it at export |
