## What the export changes

The export reads the validated blueprint and writes what awa decided at build time: the final
system prompt, the model, the tools and the limits. It re-expresses them with LangChain built-ins,
so the behavior matches (same tool calls, same approvals, same output schema) but the code is
not awa's internal stack. awa's own extras are not reproduced: tool timeouts, retries,
idempotency and result framing, prompt and result caches, run records, redaction and the
output and tool guards.
